<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Lincoln returns for an adult preventive visit, four weeks after his twelve-week depression review. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. The poison ivy rash cleared during the prednisone taper, which he finished four days ago, with no rebound. He slept more lightly on the first three nights of the 60 mg dose but had no mood change, racing thoughts, or irritability, and the nurse telephone check four days into the course found the rash improving and his sleep back to normal. His mood has stayed good, his PHQ-9 is 3 today, and he has had no suicidal thoughts. He continues sertraline 50 mg daily and misses about one dose every two weeks. He walks most evenings and is working full days. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, established patient</td></tr><tr><td>Recent illness</td><td>Poison ivy dermatitis, cleared; prednisone taper finished four days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Depression</td><td>In remission for about a month on sertraline 50 mg; PHQ-9 3</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No emergency visits, hospital stays, or injuries</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg daily; no over-the-counter medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities; working full days</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better than in the summer</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Close friend and law colleagues; values correspondence and storytelling; work stress manageable; no loneliness</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>No current tobacco or nicotine use; no alcohol; no nonprescribed drugs; walks most evenings; regular meals; sleeps about seven hours</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages his own medicines, money, and work schedule</td></tr><tr><td>Home and personal safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; wears a seat belt; access to lethal means reviewed again and unchanged since the intake review</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Asked privately; no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Vision, hearing, and dental</td><td>No vision or hearing concerns; sees a dentist yearly</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

