    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Anxiety, alcohol, drug use, and tobacco screens are negative. Blood pressure 116/70 mmHg is normal. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, in remission (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 3 today, with item 9 scored 0, after 4 at the twelve-week review: the score has stayed in the remission range for about a month, which confirms remission. The prednisone course caused only brief light sleep. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg daily for at least six months from remission, then review tapering together.</item><item>PHQ-9 every two to four weeks in the continuation phase; the next one by nurse telephone check in about four weeks.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and kept; 988 and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Poison ivy dermatitis (L23.7)</content>. Resolved after the 15-day prednisone taper, without rebound or infection. [S]<list><item>Long sleeves, trousers, and gloves for brush clearing; wash clothes and tools afterwards.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Depression screening and monitoring</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 3, with item 9 scored 0; already monitored every two to four weeks in his depression care</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GAD-7 2</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No nonprescribed drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No current tobacco or nicotine use</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>116/70 mmHg; recheck at least every three to five years</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antigen and antibody test, with his consent; no prior result on record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test with reflex RNA, with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel (surface antigen, surface antibody, and core antibody)</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>No record of a prior series; he prefers to start it when the screening panel is back</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed; he plans to get this season&apos;s vaccine at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Tdap</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Given about four and a half years ago; next booster in about five and a half years</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision for adults 27 to 45; after discussion he declined</td></tr><tr><td>Live vaccines after prednisone</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>None is due. Because he took at least 20 mg of prednisone a day for 15 days, any live vaccine would wait a month after the course</td></tr><tr><td>Healthy diet and physical activity</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walks most evenings; encouraged to keep at least 150 minutes of moderate activity a week</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and statin assessment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Statin assessment starts at 40; no cardiovascular risk factors are recorded</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>For adults 35 to 70 with overweight or obesity; his BMI is 22.4</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at 45</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1841-1842 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B results will be sent when available, with a plan for the hepatitis B vaccine. Nurse telephone PHQ-9 in about four weeks. Depression review in three months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
